.TH SEMCTL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
semctl \- control a System V semaphore set
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/sem.h>
.B int semctl(int id, int number, int command, void* argument);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Supports Linux control commands including IPC_RMID, IPC_SET, IPC_STAT,
GETVAL, GETALL and SETALL.  Pass NULL for commands without an argument.
Use semctl_value for SETVAL.  Unlike GNU libc's variadic semctl, Crunch
requires four arguments and uses separate pointer and integer interfaces.
The supplied structures have Linux x86\-64 layouts.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the command result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR semctl_value (3crunch),
.BR semget (3crunch),
.BR semctl (2)
